NAME
    write - the desktop's text editor (the video card V4)

SYNOPSIS
    write [file]

DESCRIPTION
    Edits a text file (default /write.txt; a new one if it is not
    there) in a window on the graphics screen, 78 characters by 22
    lines. The cursor is an inverted cell. The keys are the video
    card's PS/2 keyboard's:
        a character   inserted at the cursor
        Enter         a new line
        Backspace     the character before the cursor out
        Delete        the character under it out
        the arrows    move the cursor; Home and End go to the
                      line's start and end, Page Up and Page Down
                      21 lines
        Ctrl-S        save (or Save in the menu bar)
        Ctrl-Q        quit, without saving (or Quit)
    A press in the text puts the cursor there. The menu bar says
    edited after a change and saved after a save.

NOTES
    At most 4,000 characters; a line longer than 78 shows its first
    78. The finder opens a file that is not a program with write.
    Needs the video card V4 and /lib/wmk. Written 2026-11-20 after
    the P8X's write (os/lib_wm.c).
